      title: 'Linh’s work and study routine', instruction: 'Nghe hai lượt. Chưa mở script. Ghi từ khóa rồi thuật lại.',
      lines: ['LẦN 1 · Ý CHÍNH', '1. Who is speaking?', '2. What are the main topics?', 'Work, study or a family trip?', '3. Who does Linh study with?', 'LẦN 2 · CHI TIẾT', '1. How far is the hotel from home?', 'How does Linh get there?', '2. How long does the journey take?', 'What time does work start?', '3. When is her English class?', 'How long is it? How much is it?', 'Thuật lại 6–8 câu. Nêu công việc, lịch học và kế hoạch thứ Bảy.'],
      dialogue: null,
      notes: 'Read twice at 105–120 words per minute in clear American English. First gist, then details. Invite a first retell before showing the script. Answers: Linh; work and study; Mai; four kilometers / bus; fifteen minutes / eight; Tuesdays and Thursdays at six thirty / one hour / five dollars per person. SCRIPT: Hi, I’m Linh. I work at a hotel near the river in Da Nang. My home is about four kilometers from the hotel. I usually get to work by bus, and it takes about fifteen minutes. I leave home at seven and start work at eight. I like my job because I meet people from different places. On Tuesdays and Thursdays, I study English at a small café with my friend Mai. Our class starts at six thirty and lasts an hour. It costs five dollars per person. After class, we sometimes have dinner together. We prefer local food because it’s fresh and doesn’t cost much. This Saturday, we’re free in the morning. We want to join a walking tour that starts at the museum.',
